  "updateinfo_id": "ALSA-2026:89758",
  "description": "Mozilla Firefox is an open-source web browser, designed for standards compliance, performance, and portability.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * libexpat: denial of service via crafted XML input (CVE-2026-45186)\n  * expat: expat: Information disclosure via heap buffer over-read in XML_ParseBuffer (CVE-2026-77214)\n  * firefox: thunderbird: Privilege escalation in the Application Update component (CVE-2026-109704)\n  * firefox: Use-after-free in the XML component (CVE-2026-109718)\n  * firefox: Incorrect boundary conditions in the JavaScript Engine component (CVE-2026-109715)\n  * firefox: firefox: Sandbox escape via incorrect boundary conditions in Win32 widget (CVE-2026-109740)\n  * firefox: Use-after-free in the Storage: IndexedDB component (CVE-2026-109706)\n  * firefox: Use-after-free in the Crash Reporting component (CVE-2026-109713)\n  * firefox: Use-after-free in the DOM: Core \u0026 HTML component (CVE-2026-109724)\n  * firefox: Information disclosure, privilege escalation in the Security: Process Sandboxing component (CVE-2026-109709)\n  * firefox: Sandbox escape, site isolation issue due to incorrect boundary conditions, use-after-free in the Networking component (CVE-2026-109705)\n  * firefox: Use-after-free in the JavaScript Engine: JIT component (CVE-2026-109729)\n  * firefox: Incorrect boundary conditions in the JavaScript Engine component (CVE-2026-109716)\n  * firefox: Race condition, use-after-free in the Graphics: CanvasWebGL component (CVE-2026-109719)\n  * firefox: Integer overflow in the Layout: Text and Fonts component (CVE-2026-109723)\n  * firefox: Sandbox escape due to incorrect boundary conditions in the Networking component (CVE-2026-109708)\n  * firefox: Use-after-free in the DOM: Bindings (WebIDL) component (CVE-2026-109717)\n  * firefox: Sandbox escape due to use-after-free in the Networking component (CVE-2026-109707)\n  * firefox: JIT miscompilation in the JavaScript: WebAssembly component (CVE-2026-109720)\n  * firefox: Use-after-free in the SVG component (CVE-2026-109726)\n  * firefox: Integer overflow in the Graphics component (CVE-2026-109730)\n  * firefox: Use-after-free in the Audio/Video component (CVE-2026-109727)\n  * firefox: Use-after-free in the DOM: Streams component (CVE-2026-109732)\n  * firefox: Use-after-free in the DOM: Core \u0026 HTML component (CVE-2026-109725)\n  * firefox: Sandbox escape due to uninitialized memory in the Graphics component (CVE-2026-109712)\n  * firefox: Use-after-free in the Graphics: Canvas2D component (CVE-2026-109711)\n  * firefox: JIT miscompilation in the JavaScript Engine: JIT component (CVE-2026-109722)\n  * firefox: Use-after-free in the DOM: Animation component (CVE-2026-109728)\n  * firefox: Incorrect boundary conditions in the JavaScript Engine: JIT component (CVE-2026-109721)\n\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):  \n\n  * Firefox ESR 153 rebase [rhel-10.2.z] (JIRA:RHEL-175166)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n",
